    \"New security policy in effect\"`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`  ]`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`}`})}),`\n`]})})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`$schema`}),` line in the example above points to the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json`,children:`official JSON schema`}),` for Claude Code settings. Adding it to your `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`settings.json`}),` enables autocomplete and inline validation in VS Code, Cursor, and any other editor that supports JSON schema validation.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`The published schema is updated periodically and may not include settings added in the most recent CLI releases, so a validation warning on a recently documented field does not necessarily mean your configuration is invalid.`}),`\n`,_jsx(Tip,{children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`After you edit a settings file, run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/status`}),` inside Claude Code to confirm it was loaded. The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Setting sources`}),` line lists each settings source loaded for the current session; a source appears once it loads with at least one setting, so a file with broken JSON doesn’t appear even if it contains settings. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#verify-active-settings`,children:`Verify active settings`}),`.`]})}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`when-edits-take-effect`,children:`When edits take effect`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Claude Code watches your settings files and reloads them when they change, so edits to most keys apply to the running session without a restart. This includes `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`permissions`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hooks`}),`, and credential helpers like `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`apiKeyHelper`}),`. The reload covers user, project, local, and managed settings, and the `,_jsxs(_components.a,{href:`/en/hooks#configchange`,children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ConfigChange`}),` hook`]}),` fires for each detected change.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`A few keys are read once at session start and apply on the next restart instead:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`model`}),`: use `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/model-config#setting-your-model`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/model`})}),` to switch mid-session`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/output-styles`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`outputStyle`})}),`: part of the system prompt, which is rebuilt on `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/clear`}),` or restart`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`invalid-entries-in-managed-settings`,children:`Invalid entries in managed settings`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Managed settings parse tolerantly. When a managed configuration contains an entry that fails schema validation, Claude Code strips that entry, records a warning, and enforces every remaining valid policy. A single typo cannot disable the rest of your organization’s policy. Run `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/commands#all-commands`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/doctor`})}),` to list stripped entries with their source file and field.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`This behavior is consistent across all three delivery mechanisms: `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/server-managed-settings`,children:`server-managed settings`}),`, plist and registry policies deployed through MDM, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`managed-settings.json`}),` files. Requires Claude Code v2.1.169 or later.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Security-enforcement fields are handled per field instead of being stripped wholesale when they are present but invalid:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Field`}),_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Behavior when present but invalid`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedMcpServers`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Enforced as an empty allowlist, so no MCP servers are admitted until the value is fixed. An individual invalid entry is stripped and the valid subset is enforced.`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowManagedHooksOnly`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Treated as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),`, so the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#hook-configuration`,children:`hook restrictions`}),` apply until the value is fixed and, unless `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`disableCommandPluginSources`}),` is explicitly `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`false`}),`, command-sourced plugins are disabled. Applies in v2.1.229 and later.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowManagedMcpServersOnly`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Treated as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),`.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`disableCommandPluginSources`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Treated as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),`, so command-sourced plugins stay disabled until the value is fixed. Applies in v2.1.229 and later.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`availableModels`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Enforced as an empty allowlist, so only the Default model is available until the value is fixed. An individual non-string entry is stripped and the valid subset is enforced. Applies in v2.1.175 and later.`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`enforceAvailableModels`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Treated as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),`. Applies in v2.1.175 and later.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`forceLoginOrgUUID`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`No organization is permitted to log in until the value is fixed.`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deniedMcpServers`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`An individual invalid entry is stripped and the valid subset is enforced. A wholly invalid value is dropped with a warning, since denying every server would block servers the policy never named.`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sandbox.credentials`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`An invalid entry in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`files`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`envVars`}),` that still has a valid `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`path`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`name`}),` and a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode`}),` of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mask`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),`, such as one whose `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extract`}),` pattern has no capturing group, is degraded to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode: \"deny\"`}),` with a warning, so the credential stays blocked, not masked, until you fix the entry. A degraded `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`files`}),` entry pins `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#disable-filesystem-isolation`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`filesystem.disabled`})}),` like an explicit `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),` entry, and the warning notes that its read block isn’t enforced if managed settings turn filesystem isolation off. An entry with an unknown `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode`}),` or an invalid `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`path`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`name`}),` is stripped. Each case warns; whether an entry is degraded or stripped, the remaining valid entries are still enforced, and a wholly invalid `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials`}),` value is dropped while the rest of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sandbox`}),` still applies. Applies in v2.1.191 and later; before v2.1.221, every invalid entry was stripped.`]})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`requiredMinimumVersion`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`requiredMaximumVersion`}),` fail open by design: an invalid value is stripped rather than enforced, so a bad policy push cannot prevent Claude Code from starting.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Validation errors surface in three places:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`Interactive sessions show a dialog at startup listing the invalid entries.`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Headless runs with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`-p`}),` print a summary to stderr.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/debug-your-config`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude doctor`})}),` lists each invalid entry with its source and field.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Validate policy changes by running `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude doctor`}),` on a test machine before deploying them fleet-wide.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`This tolerance applies only to managed settings. User, project, and local settings files remain strict: a file that fails validation is rejected as a whole and reported.`}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`available-settings`,children:`Available settings`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`settings.json`}),` supports a number of options:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Key`}),_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Description`}),_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Example`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`advisorModel`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Model for the server-side `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/advisor`,children:`advisor tool`}),`. Accepts the model aliases `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"fable\"`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"opus\"`}),`, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"sonnet\"`}),`, or a full model ID. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"fable\"`}),` requires `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/advisor#choose-an-advisor-model`,children:`Fable 5 access`}),`. Written automatically when you run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/advisor`}),`, except when you pick Fable while the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/advisor#fable-advisor-and-usage-credits`,children:`usage-credits consent`}),` is pending. Unset to disable the advisor.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"opus\"`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`agent`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Run the main thread as a named subagent, and set the default agent for sessions dispatched from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude agents`}),`. Applies that subagent’s system prompt, tool restrictions, and model. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sub-agents#invoke-subagents-explicitly`,children:`Invoke subagents explicitly`})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"code-reviewer\"`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`agentPushNotifEnabled`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Default`}),`: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`false`}),`. When `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/remote-control`,children:`Remote Control`}),` is connected, allow Claude to send proactive push notifications to your phone, for example when a long task finishes. Appears in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/config`}),` as `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Push when Claude decides`}),`. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/remote-control#mobile-push-notifications`,children:`Mobile push notifications`})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowAllClaudeAiMcps`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`(Managed settings only) Load the claude.ai connectors Claude Code fetches itself alongside a deployed `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`managed-mcp.json`}),`, which otherwise takes exclusive control and suppresses them. Connectors delivered to cloud sessions stay suppressed. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/managed-mcp#allow-claude-ai-connectors-alongside-the-managed-set`,children:`Managed MCP configuration`})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedChannelPlugins`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`(Managed settings only) Allowlist of channel plugins that may push messages. Replaces the default Anthropic allowlist when set. Undefined = fall back to the default, empty array = block all channel plugins. Requires `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`channelsEnabled: true`}),`. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/channels#restrict-which-channel-plugins-can-run`,children:`Restrict which channel plugins can run`})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[{ \"marketplace\": \"claude-plugins-official\", \"plugin\": \"telegram\" }]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedHttpHookUrls`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Allowlist of URL patterns that HTTP hooks may target. Supports `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`*`}),` as a wildcard. When set, hooks with non-matching URLs are blocked. Undefined = no restrictions, empty array = block all HTTP hooks. Arrays merge across settings sources. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#hook-configuration`,children:`Hook configuration`})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[\"https://hooks.example.com/*\"]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedMcpServers`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`When set in managed-settings.json, allowlist of MCP servers 