warning. Can’t be combined with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extract`}),`. Accepted but ignored when `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode`}),` is `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),`. Requires Claude Code v2.1.224 or later.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"jwt\"`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials.envVars[].maskClaims`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Top-level payload claims to mask inside the decoded JWT instead of replacing the whole token. Requires `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`decode`}),` and at least one non-empty claim name. Behaves like `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials.files[].maskClaims`}),`, except that when no named claim matches, the variable passes through unmasked with a warning. Requires Claude Code v2.1.224 or later.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[\"api_key\"]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials.envVars[].injectHosts`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Hosts where the sandbox proxy substitutes the real value of a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mask`}),` entry. The proxy injects only on connections `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowedDomains`}),` admits, so each destination must also pass that list. When unset, the proxy substitutes the value on requests to every host in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowedDomains`}),`. Write an IPv6 destination as the bare canonical compressed address, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"::1\"`}),`, not the bracketed form. See `,_jsxs(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#ipv6-destinations-in-injecthosts`,children:[`IPv6 destinations in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`injectHosts`})]}),` for what each list matches. Accepted but ignored when `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mode`}),` is `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),`. Requires Claude Code v2.1.199 or later.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[\"api.github.com\"]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials.allowPlaintextInject`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Allow `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mask`}),` substitution on plain HTTP requests as well as TLS-terminated HTTPS. On plain HTTP the upstream identity is unverified and the credential travels in cleartext, so leave this off outside trusted test networks. Only honored from user, managed, or CLI `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--settings`}),` settings, not from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.json`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.local.json`}),`. Default: false. Requires Claude Code v2.1.199 or later.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials.awsPairs`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Groups of masked environment variables that form one AWS credential for `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#re-sign-aws-requests`,children:`SigV4 re-signing`}),`, for non-standard variable names; Claude Code links the conventional `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`}),`, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`AWS_SESSION_TOKEN`}),` trio automatically when those variables are masked whole-value. Each entry names the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials.envVars`}),` entry holding each part in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`accessKeyIdVar`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`secretAccessKeyVar`}),`, and optionally `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sessionTokenVar`}),`. Each named variable must be a whole-value `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mask`}),` entry, without `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extract`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`decode`}),`, and can fill only one slot across all pairs. Only honored from user, managed, or CLI `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--settings`}),` settings. Requires Claude Code v2.1.224 or later.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[{ \"accessKeyIdVar\": \"MY_KEY_ID\", \"secretAccessKeyVar\": \"MY_SECRET_KEY\" }]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`credentials.sigv4`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Policies for AWS request forms the sandbox proxy `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#re-sign-aws-requests`,children:`can’t re-sign`}),`: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`streaming`}),` for aws-chunked streaming uploads, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`presigned`}),` for presigned URLs, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`sigv4a`}),` for SigV4A asymmetric signatures. Each accepts `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deny`}),`, the default, which fails the request at the proxy, or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`passthrough`}),`, which forwards the request with its signature computed from the masked placeholder, so AWS rejects it. Applies only to requests signed with a masked pair’s placeholder access key ID. Only honored from user, managed, or CLI `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--settings`}),` settings. Requires Claude Code v2.1.224 or later.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`{ \"streaming\": \"passthrough\" }`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowUnixSockets`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`(macOS only) Unix socket paths accessible in sandbox. Ignored on Linux and WSL2, where the seccomp filter cannot inspect socket paths; use `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowAllUnixSockets`}),` instead.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[\"~/.ssh/agent-socket\"]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowAllUnixSockets`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Allow all Unix socket connections in sandbox. On Linux and WSL2, when the optional `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#set-up-linux-and-wsl2`,children:`seccomp filter`}),` is installed, this is the only way to permit Unix sockets, since it skips the filter that otherwise blocks `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`socket(AF_UNIX, ...)`}),` calls; without the filter, the sandbox doesn’t block Unix-socket calls. On WSL2, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),` also reopens the interop socket that launches Windows binaries. Default: false`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowLocalBinding`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Allow binding to localhost ports (macOS only). Default: false`}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowMachLookup`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Additional XPC/Mach service names the sandbox may look up (macOS only). Supports a single trailing `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`*`}),` for prefix matching. Needed for tools that communicate via XPC such as the iOS Simulator or Playwright.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[\"com.apple.coresimulator.*\"]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowedDomains`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Array of domains to allow for outbound network traffic. Supports wildcards, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`*.example.com`}),`. Write IPv6 literals bracketed, with an optional port: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"[::1]\"`}),` allows every port and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"[::1]:443\"`}),` one port. The bracketed form requires Claude Code v2.1.229 or later. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#ipv6-addresses-in-domain-lists`,children:`IPv6 addresses in domain lists`}),`.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[\"github.com\", \"*.npmjs.org\"]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.deniedDomains`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Array of domains to block for outbound network traffic. Supports the same wildcard syntax as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedDomains`}),`. For IPv6 literals, see `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#ipv6-addresses-in-domain-lists`,children:`IPv6 addresses in domain lists`}),`. Takes precedence over `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedDomains`}),` when both match. Merged from all settings sources regardless of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowManagedDomainsOnly`}),`.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`[\"sensitive.cloud.example.com\"]`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.strictAllowlist`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Deny sandboxed commands access to hosts outside the allowlist instead of prompting for approval. The allowlist is `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedDomains`}),` plus domains from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`WebFetch(domain:...)`}),` allow rules, or only the managed settings entries when `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowManagedDomainsOnly`}),` is set. Enforced for sandboxed commands only; in-process tools such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`WebFetch`}),` aren’t gated by this setting. Only honored from user, managed, or CLI `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--settings`}),` settings, not from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.json`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.local.json`}),`. Default: false. Requires Claude Code v2.1.219 or later. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#network-isolation`,children:`Network isolation`})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.allowManagedDomainsOnly`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`(Managed settings only) Only `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowedDomains`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`WebFetch(domain:...)`}),` allow rules from managed settings are respected. Domains from user, project, and local settings are ignored. Non-allowed domains are blocked automatically without prompting the user. Denied domains are still respected from all sources. Default: false`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.httpProxyPort`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`HTTP proxy port used if you wish to bring your own proxy. If not specified, Claude will run its own proxy.`}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`8080`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.socksProxyPort`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`SOCKS5 proxy port used if you wish to bring your own proxy. If not specified, Claude will run its own proxy.`}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`8081`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`network.tlsTerminate`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Experimental. Terminate TLS inside the sandbox proxy so it can read the contents of HTTPS requests. Required for `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mask`}),` `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sandboxing#mask-credentials`,children:`credential substitution`}),`. Set `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`{}`}),` to generate an ephemeral certificate authority for the session, or set `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`caCertPath`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`caKeyPath`}),` to use your own. Only honored from user, managed, or CLI `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--settings`}),` settings, not from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.json`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.local.json`}),`. Requires Claude Code v2.1.199 or later.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`{}`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`enableWeakerNestedSandbox`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Enable weaker sandbox for unprivileged Docker environments (Linux and WSL2 only). `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Reduces security.`}),` Default: false`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`enableWeakerNetworkIsolation`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`(macOS only) Allow access to the system TLS trust service (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`com.apple.trustd.agent`}),`) in the sandbox. Required for Go-based tools like `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`gh`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`gcloud`}),`, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`terraform`}),` to verify TLS certificates when using `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`httpProxyPort`}),` with a MITM proxy and custom CA. `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Reduces security`}),` by opening a potential data exfiltration path. Default: false`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`allowAppleEvents`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`(macOS only) Allow sandboxed commands to send Apple Events. Required for `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`open`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`osascript`}),`, and tools that open URLs in a browser, which otherwise fail with error `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`-600`}),`. `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Removes code-execution isolation.`}),` Sandboxed commands can launch other applications unsandboxed with no user prompt; they can also send AppleScript commands to running applications such as Terminal, subject to the per-app macOS automation-consent prompt (TCC). Only honored from user, managed, or CLI settings, not from project settings. Default: false`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ripgrep`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Custom `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ripgrep`}),` binary for the sandbox. Set `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`command`}),` to the binary’s path. To pass arguments to that binary, also set `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`args`}),`. If you don’t set `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ripgrep`}),`, the sandbox uses the same `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ripgrep`}),` binary as Claude Code. That is the bundled binary unless you set `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/env-vars`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`USE_BUILTIN_RIPGREP`})}),` to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`0`}),`. Only honored from user, managed, or CLI settings.`]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`{ \"command\": \"/usr/local/bin/rg\", \"args\": [\"--no-config\"] }`})})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`bwrapPath`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`(Managed settings only, Linux/WSL2) Absolute path to the bubblewrap (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`bwrap`}),`) binary. Overrides automatic detection via `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PATH`}),`. Only honored from `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/settings#settings-precedence`,children:`managed settings`}),`, not from user or project settings. Useful when `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`bwrap`}),` is installed at a non-standard location in managed environments.`]}),_jsx(_components.td